{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>To commit a trespass against HaShem.</b> The Kabbalah has already explained that this is said regarding robbery of a convert, for indeed one who robs him profanes the name of his Elohim in the eyes of the convert who came to take refuge under His wings; therefore it is called trespass against the sacred, and he is liable to a guilt-offering according to the law of every trespass against Him."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:42.062775467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}